{"agent":"fx-bugs-phase-done-orphans","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`standing.removed` is only special-cased when `n == 1`. State with `bugs` done and a `bugs-2` item present with `removed=True` but not `terminal`: the loop reaches n=2, the guard does not fire, and the `else` branch calls `_open_phase_of(st, \"bugs-2\")`. `_open_phase_of` is documented to return `\"\"` only when the phase is done; a removed, non-terminal phase is returned as open, so `parent` becomes `\"bugs-2\"`, filing the fix task under a removed phase and re-creating the orphan bug for removed follow-up phases.","digest":"b73ff0f0a6285e5b","location":"ddflow/api/knowledge/bugs.py:264","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/knowledge/bugs.py:264"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The assertion `parent.id not in (\"bugs\", \"bugs-2\")` is over-constrained. The change’s own intent says a valid fix may “reopen/recreate a bugs phase.” For the exact input this test constructs (`bugs` done plus removed `bugs-2`), a correct implementation that reopens the standing `bugs` phase yields `parent.id == \"bugs\"` with `parent.removed == False` and `parent.terminal == False`; this test would fail even though the bug is fixed. The test should verify that the parent is an open, non-removed bugs phase, not forbid the allowed `\"bugs\"` id.","digest":"382190edc0a6f637","location":"tests/test_bugs_phase_done_orphans.py:test_a_removed_followup_phase_is_skipped","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_bugs_phase_done_orphans.py:test_a_removed_followup_phase_is_skipped"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":1,"delta_from":"0a509df7f4d947feebaeae95cca8dc17c451ef9e","delta_raised":["382190edc0a6f637"],"delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":888,"diff_sha":"216f727c732ec161c986bae4af1a25a72ba7a79d566d6ba01534e8a78a690ab6","diff_source":"delta review of 1 commit since 0a509df7f4","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"un